{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "Heaven's Appraisal keeps Gavels from being dodged (#8865)",
 "contract": "Heaven's Appraisal 300353 (Level 40 passive) reads \"Your Gavels can no longer be missed, dodged, or parried\". Gavel of Light 800611, Grace 800614 and Wrath 800617 are SpellFamilyName 33, SpellFamilyFlags[1] 32 melee-class spells. Effect 0 of 300353 is a flat SPELLMOD_RESIST_MISS_CHANCE of +1000 on that mask, which Unit::MeleeSpellMissChance applies to the Gavel's hit chance, so misses were already removed. Effects 1 and 2 are flat modifiers for other spells and the Sun Cleric contract turned them into dummies, so nothing stopped Unit::MeleeSpellHitResult from rolling dodge and parry; SPELL_AURA_IGNORE_COMBAT_RESULT is the native aura for that (MiscValue 2 dodge, 4 parry) and only affects spells its class mask names. The contract now turns effects 1 and 2 of 300353 into those two auras on mask [0,32,0]. Two level 60 Horde warriors with PvP on stand in for the targets, each carrying Evasion 5277 (+50% dodge, re-applied before every round because it lasts only 15 seconds), so the target also keeps its native parry. The Sun Cleric with 300353 casts Gavel of Light 20 times and every cast must deal damage (a dodge deals none); the control Sun Cleric without it hits an identically dodging target and must be dodged at least once (the target's dodge chance is 41.9%, so 20 straight hits has a chance near 0.002%). Parry takes the same path through the same aura (MiscValue 4); the warrior's parry rides along in the same twelve casts but is not isolated.",
 "timeout_ms": 240000,
